      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The 2014 Multiple Myeloma (MM) Mentorship Program provided a focused, interactive, peer-to-peer educational experience, including updates in MM, for 10 mentees that led to advanced clinical educator status."
        },
        {
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "The objective of the program was (a) to improve mentees' knowledge, competency, confidence, and level of performance in the management of MM and (b) to build speaking expertise."
        },
        {
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "From May 2014 to March 2015, 10 mentees were educated on MM with a structured serial learning curriculum. Mentees then presented slide decks, and modular activities were opened to a national audience of professionals. Pre- and post-test surveys were compiled, and a RealIndex® composite score was calculated."
        },
        {
          "Label": "FINDINGS",
          "content": "Gains were measured across the curriculum in learning domains of knowledge, confidence, and practice strategy. Pre-/post-test scores show that the mentorship cohort's average scores on knowledge, confidence, and performance were higher compared to the national program."
        }
      ]},
